{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and motion primitives, separating sensing and action. The specification enforces conservative, deterministic exploration: random_walk is used for coverage in clear states, move_forward is only allowed in a short commit state, and obstacle events force immediate turn-based recovery. Recovery states deterministically select a single turn direction based on obstacle location, and no obstacle state allows forward or random_walk actions. Full_rotate is only available in a deliberate scan state. All uncontrollable events are total in every state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception (sensing) and motion (actuation) into distinct plant automata for clarity and modularity.",
    "Specification automaton enforces safe, conservative exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward only in commit, deterministic turn recovery after obstacles, and no forward/random_walk in obstacle states."
  ],
